  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 AM MDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nMain focus over the next couple of days will be a low pressure \nsystem that is currently over Oregon. This system will bring \nrounds of showers and thunderstorms to the area starting this \nafternoon and continuing through Saturday. Coverage this \nafternoon and this evening looks very isolated. But this system \nwill be tapping into some monsoon moisture and advecting that \nnorthward late tonight into Thursday. This will produce good \nchances for showers and thunderstorms for Thursday and Friday. \nBy Saturday, the low will be moving through our area and into \nWyoming. This will shift the better chances for showers into the\neastern highlands. In terms of qpf, this doesn't appear to be \nan overly exciting storm. Most areas will probably see less than\n0.25 inches over the course of the next few days. QPF over the \neastern highlands may perform a little better with up to 0.50 \ninches possible.",
